Video controls are in the **Output** inspector. The **General** section chooses the output container; the **Video** section controls encoding. Available options depend on the source, selected container, and detected encoders.

## Container and codec

A container holds video, audio, subtitle tracks, and metadata. A codec describes how an individual stream is encoded.

Frame can export MP4, MKV, WebM, MOV, M2T, MTS, M2TS, and GIF. Video encoders include H.264, H.265, VP9, AV1, ProRes, and MPEG-2 where the selected container supports them.

Use MP4 with H.264 as a practical starting point for general playback. If you choose a newer codec or a different pixel format, verify that the destination player supports it.

<DocsScreenshot
  scene="video-output"
